      "confidence": 0.75,
      "curator_note": "cis-1,3-cyclohexanediol diacetate protonated on one acetate carbonyl (arrow label 'id'). Neighbouring-group participation: the OTHER (neutral) acetate's carbonyl oxygen O9 displaces the protonated acetate from ring carbon C3, expelling it as neutral acetic acid and closing a 2-methyl-1,3-dioxan-2-ylium (acetoxonium) bridge across the cis-1,3-diaxial positions C1/C3. Book draws 2 arcs: (i) the neutral-acetate carbonyl pi (C8=O9) forming the new O9-C3 bond, and (ii) the ester oxygen O11 of the leaving acetate forming that fragment's new C12=O11 carbonyl. Move <3> (the protonated carbonyl pi C12=O13 collapsing to an O13 lone pair, which neutralises O13-H+ to the acetic-acid hydroxyl) is an implicit heterolytic step required for electron balance (not drawn on the page). The product cation is drawn with '+' on the central bridge carbon C8 (localised carbenium O-C+-O form chosen here; it is resonance-delocalised over O7/O9 as the two oxocarbenium forms)."
    },
